  "body": "Part of #874. Found while working #874 (PR #1804). Related: #320, #303, #1595.\n\n**What happens now.** The program walk (`crates/app/src/stock_sim_carry.rs`, `walk`) takes a verdict of the stock before it leaves the walk's sight, and keeps the gouges for the final verdict (`keep_gouges`, `fold_left`):\n\n- when a later setup takes a new block (#320);\n- when the stock is turned side-on (#874, PR #1804).\n\nThat verdict is `judge`: the stock against the parts. It does not apply `credit_breaks` (#303) or `credit_marks` (#1595). The final verdict applies them only for the operations of the last setup (`program_breaks`, `program_marks` in `stock_sim.rs`).\n\n**The risk.** A chamfer, a deburr, an Engrave or a Trace in the earlier setup cuts below the model by design. The kept verdict can count that cut as a gouge, and the post gate then refuses a correct program. This was not reproduced with a fixture; it follows from the code. The first step is a test that shows it.\n\n**The work.** Apply the breaks and the marks of the earlier setup's operations to the verdict that `walk` takes before a new block or a side-on turn.\n\n**Done means:** a program with a chamfer in Setup1 and a side-on (or new-block) Setup2 reads no gouge for the chamfer; a real gouge in Setup1 still reads; a pinning test for each.\n",
